  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would be useful to have a ForEach node that takes a collection as input, executes the body flow node like the For loop, but provides the object to the body instead of just the index, and potentially the index of the object if that's already required internally. \n\nThis is just a slightly easier way to go through a collection without calling GetValue each time. If Dictionary<T>, HashSet<T>, or other collections without indexers are implemented this would be necessary to iterate their contents.",
